          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "Implemented the MoonBit INI parser and verified it end to end.\n\n**Implementation**\n- [ini.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/ini.mbt) — error type, LF/CRLF line splitting, main parse loop, continuation joining\n- [chars.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/chars.mbt) — character predicates and array helpers\n- [values.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/values.mbt) — section headers, entries, quoted/unquoted values, escape tables\n- [printer.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/printer.mbt) — round-trip-safe printing\n- [ini_behavior_test.mbt](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/ini_behavior_test.mbt) — additional conformance tests\n- [README.md](D:/a/openseek-swe-agi/openseek-swe-agi/tasks/ini_run_1/README.md) — architecture, parsing rules, usage, and design notes\n\n**Behavior covered**\n- Global entries and named sections, including repeated headers and last-wins duplicates\n- First `=` or `:` separator, with later separators treated as value text\n- Full-line and inline `;`/`#` comments, disabled inside quotes\n- Double/single-quoted values, per-carrier escape tables, escaped quotes, text-after-quote rejection\n- Backslash continuations with the odd/even trailing-run rule, continuation text as literal text\n- Bare `\\r`/CRLF handling, Unicode, leading/trailing whitespace\n- Rejection of malformed headers, empty/control-character keys, unterminated or mismatched quotes, and invalid continuations\n- `parse(print(doc)) == doc` across generated documents and a character-grid stress test\n\n**Validation**\n- `moon test` → **47/47 passed** (12 public + 35 added)\n- `moon check` → **0 errors**; the remaining warnings all originate in the protected files `ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, and `ini_pub_test.mbt`\n- Protected files were restored to their original content (verified with `diff --strip-trailing-cr` against the pristine template)\n- An independent review found no blockers; its one substantive finding — a separator arriving via a continuation line — was fixed and covered by a new test.\n\n```openseek-file\nREADME.md\n```"
