          "kind": "finished",
          "message": "All work is complete. Final verification: **100/100 tests pass, 0 compiler errors**, and only the 7 pre-existing warnings from the protected files/manifest remain.\n\n## What I built\n\nA complete INI parser/printer in MoonBit for the dialect in [`specs/ini.md`](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\specs\\ini.md), organized by responsibility:\n\n| File | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| [scanner.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\scanner.mbt) | character classes, LF/CRLF line splitting, trimming, section-header scanning, per-carrier escape decoding, inline-comment stripping |\n| [parser.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\parser.mbt) | line walk, first-separator rule, quoted/unquoted value parsing, backslash continuations, document assembly |\n| [printer.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\printer.mbt) | serialization (every value as a double-quoted, escaped string) |\n| [error.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\error.mbt) | `IniError(line, message)` + `Show` |\n| [ini_extra_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_2\\ini_extra_test.mbt) | 88 spec-derived conformance tests |\n\nKey implementation points: scanning works on `Array[Char]` so non-ASCII indices are always valid; a trailing `\\` continuation is decided on raw text *before* escapes (the spec's odd/even run-length rule), joins the next line verbatim, and consumes it; `;`/`#` are comments only after whitespace (or whole-line); quoted values close on their own line and decode only their carrier's escapes; sections reopen and duplicate keys take their last value via direct map mutation. `print` quotes every value, which makes `parse(print(doc)) == doc` hold for unrestricted values (confirmed by 3000-case round-trip and 3000 random-string no-panic fuzzing during development).\n\nValidation run: `moon check` → 0 errors (7 pre-existing warnings in `ini_spec.mbt`/`ini_qc.mbt`/`ini_pub_test.mbt`/`moon.pkg`, untouched), `moon test` → 100 passed. An independent audit probed ~140 spec-derived inputs plus 8000 fuzz strings and found no panics and no rule violations — only genuine spec ambiguities (trailing blanks after a marker, comment glued to a closing quote, indent of continuation lines), each of which follows the most literal reading of `specs/ini.md` and is documented in the README along with the architecture, algorithm, and design decisions.\n\n```openseek-file\nREADME.md\n```"
        }
