          "message": "All work is complete and verified. Final summary:\n\n## What I built\n\nA genuine INI parser (no fixture lookups) for the dialect in `specs/ini.md`, in six focused root-package files:\n\n| File | Role |\n|---|---|\n| [chars.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\chars.mbt) | char classes + bounds-safe `Array[Char]` helpers |\n| [line_scanner.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\line_scanner.mbt) | line splitting (LF/CRLF), cursor, inline comments, trailing-backslash runs |\n| [value.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\value.mbt) | three value carriers, escape table, quoted scanning, continuations |\n| [parser.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\parser.mbt) | `parse`: line loop, section headers, entries, key validation |\n| [printer.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\printer.mbt) | `print`: quoted encoding, section-name quoting, stable ordering |\n| [error.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\error.mbt) | `priv suberror` with line-numbered messages |\n\n```diago\ndirection: right\ntext: \"StringView\"\nchars: \"Array[Char]\"\nlines: \"physical lines\"\nloop: \"line loop\"\nvalue: \"value sub-parser\"\ndoc: \"Doc\"\ntext -> chars -> lines -> loop\nloop -> value\nloop -> doc\n```\n\nKey ordering rules the parser enforces: comment stripping on the **first** line of a value only; continuation decided on **raw** text (odd backslash run = marker, even = escaped literals); trimming **before** escape decoding (so `k=a\\t` keeps its tab); quoted values never span lines and only layout/a comment may follow the closing quote.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `moon test` → **46 tests, 46 passed, 0 failed** (12 public, incl. both property tests; 34 added).\n- [ini_edge_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_edge_test.mbt) pins the escape table per carrier, the N=1…4 continuation table, CRLF, section-name quoting/re-opening, first-separator-wins, and every error class.\n- [ini_robustness_test.mbt](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\ini_robustness_test.mbt) exhaustively parses every string of length ≤ 3 over `[ ] = : ; # \" ' \\ \\n \\r space tab a` plus all ordered triples of 15 line shapes — nothing panics, and anything accepted satisfies `parse(print(doc)) == doc`.\n- `moon check`: **0 errors**; the 7 remaining warnings are all pre-existing in the protected skeleton files (`ini_spec.mbt`, `ini_qc.mbt`, `ini_pub_test.mbt`, `moon.pkg`) — none in my code.\n- `moon fmt` run over the tree and `moon info` regenerated `pkg.generated.mbti`, whose public surface is exactly `parse`, `print`, `Doc`.\n- I restored `ini_spec.mbt` to its original text after `moon fmt` migrated its `derive(...)` syntax (protected file), so `moon fmt --check` reports only that file as unformatted-by-migration.\n\nTest helpers were renamed (`edge_parse`, `edge_global_value`, `robust_try_parse`, `robust_enumerate`) so my added test files cannot collide with the withheld `ini_priv_test.mbt` in the shared black-box test package.\n\n[README.md](D:\\a\\openseek-swe-agi\\openseek-swe-agi\\tasks\\ini_run_3\\README.md) documents architecture, algorithms, usage, testing and the rationale behind each ambiguous dialect decision (trailing-newline continuations, comment-marker whitespace rule, always-quoted printing, map-order independence)."
